{"tool_name":"g3viz","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"G3viz","home":"https://cran.r-project.org/package=g3viz","license":"MIT","summary":"R package to interactively visualize genetic mutation data using a lollipop-diagram.","addition_date":"2019-08-11T08:40:47Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:24Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:G3viz","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"g3viz.group@gmail.com","name":"Xin Guo","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/g3viz/g3viz.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Variant classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3225"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"G3viz","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btz631","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 The Author(s) 2019. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.The lollipop-diagram is one of the widely used graphical representations to visualize and explore translational effects of genetic mutations in cancer genomics. However, an easy-to-use lollipop-diagram tool with full functionality is still lacking. Here, we introduce g3viz, an R package that enables researchers to explore genetic mutation data using a lollipop-diagram in a web browser. With a few lines of R code, users can interactively visualize data details, annotate findings and export resultant diagrams in high-quality figures. Because of usefulness and usability, g3viz can be generally exploited by researchers with different levels of bioinformatics skills and programming experience.","authors":[{"name":"Ge D."},{"name":"Guo X."},{"name":"Zeng W."},{"name":"Zhang B."},{"name":"Zhao S."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2